<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Airlines to issue $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Philippine Airlines to issue $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Airlines Inc will issue $200 million worth of Floating Rate Treasury Notes due in 2000 later this month, according to company documents submitted on Tuesday to the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The airline has requested the commission to exempt the notes from registration in the Philippines since these will be sold outside the country.</p>
<p>The net proceeds of $197 million are to be used for general corporate purposes, the documents showed.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937  </p>
